IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cda-public`

-- Civil Defence Act 1986, ss 101A-101C, 102, 103, 103A-103D, 105, 106, 106A, 107, 108, 111, 112 -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_civil-defence-act-1986.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

§ `ss 101A, 101B`

#ASSERT `the actor may exercise the day-to-day power` `the Commissioner` `requiring a medical examination after hazmat exposure` TRUE
#ASSERT `the actor may exercise the day-to-day power` `a member authorised by the Commissioner` `seizing contaminated things` TRUE
#ASSERT `the actor may exercise the day-to-day power` `a member authorised by the Commissioner` `closing a road` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the actor may exercise the day-to-day power` `a member not so authorised` `entering or breaking into premises` TRUE
#ASSERT `the actor may exercise the day-to-day power` `an ambulance contractor's employee` `entering or breaking into premises` TRUE
#ASSERT `the actor may exercise the day-to-day power` `an ambulance contractor's employee` `taking an unidentified unconscious person's fingerprints` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the actor may exercise the day-to-day power` `an ambulance contractor's employee` `requiring a medical examination after hazmat exposure` TRUE
#ASSERT `the actor may exercise the day-to-day power` `an SAF serviceman attached to the Force` `cutting off gas, water or electricity` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the actor may exercise the day-to-day power` `an SAF serviceman attached to the Force` `seizing contaminated things` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the actor may exercise the day-to-day power` `a police officer` `closing a road` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the actor may exercise the day-to-day power` `the Commissioner` `closing a road` FALSE

